firegeowall for Debian
======================

The package installs the binary, the systemd units and the service user `fgw`,
but enables nothing. The filter only works once nftables jumps into the chain
fgw owns, and that hook chain belongs to you.

1. Add the hook chain to your nftables configuration. Example (adjust the
   interface name):

     /usr/share/doc/firegeowall/examples/50-firegeowall.conf

   or print the snippet that matches your config.yml:

     fgw check --print-nft

   Debian's default /etc/nftables.conf does not include /etc/nftables.d/;
   add an `include "/etc/nftables.d/*.conf"` line if you use that directory.
   Then reload nftables.

2. Choose countries (config: /etc/firegeowall/config.yml, empty by default):

     fgw add CN RU

3. Fetch the lists once, then enable boot restore and the weekly refresh:

     systemctl start fgw-update.service
     systemctl enable --now fgw-restore.service fgw-update.timer
     fgw check && fgw status

Full documentation: https://github.com/TZERO78/firegeowall/tree/main/docs

Removing the package stops and disables the units. The sets and rules stay in
the running ruleset until nftables is reloaded or restarted. Purging also
deletes /etc/firegeowall and /var/lib/firegeowall; the user `fgw` is kept.
